From c6b9995e01bbfce0919681f9d89f97cb4d1fcfea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marko Tombak <84014+mxxm-t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 06:15:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spec: couple the drafter's prompt replay to target prefill
 progress (+74% prefill)

During target prefill the DSpark drafter replayed the whole prompt after
the target finished - prefill wall was 92% drafter waits. The drafter now
polls how many rows the target has completed (cudaEventQuery mapped for
HIP) and replays just those, batched. The persistent layer tap is ordered
by its event instead of a scheduler stall, and the decode-side tap wait
is per-event on GPU backends only. The eager gather keeps a full
llama_synchronize: an earlier ubatch's readiness event can pass while
this ubatch's embd_layer_inp copy is still in flight, and the wide sync
costs nothing (23.4 vs 23.3 tg).

DeepSeek-V4-Flash MXFP4 over 8 MI50 -sm layer: prefill +74% at default
-b, +64% at 100k (+217% vs the uncoupled drafter). Decode unchanged,
verify decides every emitted token. LLAMA_DSPARK_OPPORTUNISTIC=0
restores the deferred replay.
